WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:03.980
I heard Zoology was all up in arms.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.020
I didn't think Sir Kharadron
would be assassinated.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.070
There are so many obsessed people
seeking to take his place.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:17.490
To the point where idiots cling
onto my elder brother for help.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.910
So, how is he holding up?

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.250
My elder brother is still infatuated
with the Holy Grail War as always.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.750
The Greater Grail of Fuyuki, huh?

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.590
Seven Mages seeking
the omnipotent wish granter

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.510
summon seven Servants to fight.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.010
Avenging what happened ten years ago?

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.640
Or seeking vengeance
for his mentor Kayneth?

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.100
A curious man he is.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.940
Something wrong?

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:50.520
No. I just thought it was a bit strange.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:52.570
The Greater Grail...

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.570
If it really exists,

00:00:54.820 --> 00:01:00.580
even a local Magecraft ritual in the Far East
would've made a bigger commotion.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:05.160
For one Lord to have died,
it is indeed a bit quiet.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.250
Same for your
Spiritual Evocation Department.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.670
Considering that the director's
daughter died, right?

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:16.090
Is someone squelching information?

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:17.970
It's simply speculation.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.100
But it was careless of you
to not arrive at that conclusion.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:27.060
Well, we'll have my dear elder brother
go through all the hardships.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.950
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.570
Flat, you are such a...

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:06.950
What was wrong with using pyrite
because I didn't have rock salt?

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:08.200
Everything about it!

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.330
In a class to create a spell
to put up a bounded field,

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.960
why would you create a spell
to destroy it?

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.590
It's true that both rock salt
and pyrite have cubic crystals

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.420
and symbolize the realm of Earth.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:24.720
But pyrite also has a Fire element,
seen by the "pyre" within its name!

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:27.220
There it is, his ultimate, the Iron Claw!

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.680
If you had continued the ritual,
you wouldn't have created a bounded field,

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.890
I want you to hold me, sir!

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.690
but instead ruined the surrounding
mana balance and let it run wild!

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:36.270
He's still nowhere close
to the eminence of Flitz Von Erik.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.730
In the first place, if you toss pyrite
into nitric acid, you'd create poison gas!

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.730
You sure know your pro wrestling.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.530
Any lady should know about wrestling.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:41.900
Nevertheless...

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.870
I give up! I give up, sir!

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.330
You... Damn you!

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.410
Each and every time, you lavishly use
your talent to do as you please!

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:55.170
If my past self had talent like yours,

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.290
I would be...

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:00.920
Sir?

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:08.010
Ow! Ouch!

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:09.560
I lost myself there.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.390
I'll continue with the lecture.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:16.060
Now, about the balance of the field
in a realm of justice...

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.150
What is with that miserable state
Lord El-Melloi II is in?

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.030
I-I apologize.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:27.240
I came all the way from Finland
to attend a lecture!

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:33.120
But if he's like that, I can't call him
Luviagelita Edelfelt's tutor!

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:37.170
What happened to the brilliance
he showed at the Separation Castle?

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.420
Answer me, Gray.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.420
A-Actually...

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.590
A tearoom closed down?

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:46.510
Huh?

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:53.060
Yes. His favorite tearoom closed down
due to electrical malfunction.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:57.190
I know the English love their tea,
but all this over a tearoom...

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:02.570
There are no other shops
where he can eat around his house.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:06.410
To write papers, for me to buy lunch...

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:10.370
His work just doesn't progress
without that place.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.160
That's the reason?

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.620
That is the shabbiest thing
in the Clock Tower's history!

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:20.290
But he said he was going to go ask
the shopkeeper about his circumstances tonight,

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:21.920
so I'm sure...

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.300
I'm counting on you.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:26.680
Jeez!

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:34.810
Reines!

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.440
May I have a moment,
young lady of Edelfelt?

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.940
It's about the Holy Grail War.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.280
This is terrible.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.860
I think it's a rat.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:50.660
Apparently, there's an electrical leak.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:54.540
The electric bill is for a sum
we'd rather not think about.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.160
A rodent?

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.000
No. What about the public office?

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:03.380
We consulted them, but well,
they don't know how long it will take.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.880
So, we hired rodent control, but...

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:06.760
What happened?

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.720
One went missing.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:14.930
The other said he saw
something horrible,

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:18.190
and wants to do
any other job but this one.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.270
I see.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.650
Can I check things out a bit?

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.410
This is Zoology Magecraft.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.660
Electricity is leaking from here.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.910
No, it's being absorbed.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.040
A furry creature.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.120
Electricity.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:40.420
Blue.

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:42.710
So, that's what this means.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:49.340
Have you figured something out?

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:52.550
Yeah. I've identified the main issue.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:54.390
I'm going to head down right now.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:57.980
Do college professors
really go that far?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.140
And if something
were to happen to you, too...

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:08.190
If this shop stays closed,
I cause trouble to my apprentices.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.660
A sewer system from the 19th century.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.590
It's larger than I expected.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.130
No. Is it growing?

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:37.010
A lightning bounded field, huh?

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.770
So, some Mage's workshop
is down here after all.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:44.940
Sewer system, workshop and lightning.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.360
Brings back memories.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.240
Sir...

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:01.660
Hello?

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.380
Sir is...

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.340
Amazing! You're amazing, freshman!

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:10.170
So, this is what you call the Internet!

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.090
Caules, was it? You're the best!

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.510
It's nothing unusual, though.

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:19.970
Well, we were too scared
to touch Flat's PC.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:21.350
What, what?

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:23.100
Oh, it's a new model PC!

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:24.310
Is it amazing?

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.270
And he has multiple monitors!

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:28.730
This is a great unit!
Did you make it yourself?

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:29.940
Y-Yeah.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.650
It's specialized for searching
and database management.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:34.070
I hooked monitors up through a LAN.

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.280
So cool! I'm jealous!
What GPU do you have?

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:38.870
Huh?

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.450
Hello, this is Flat.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.080
Oh, Gray?

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.500
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.000
He just said "Gray-tan."

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.960
Sir hasn't returned yet?

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:52.010
I got a call from the tearoom.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:55.840
They said Sir went down into the sewer system
and hasn't returned.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.640
Yeah, okay, I got it!

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.890
Don't worry, leave the rest to me.
I'll head over right away.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:01.970
See you!

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:02.890
Why?

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.560
Why isn't it me? Why do you
get a phone call from Gray-tan?

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:08.150
Tell me right now!

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.820
To hear Gray-tan's voice
right close to your ear...

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:11.820
Hey, stop it!
You'll break my computer!

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.860
Give me that ear! I'm so jealous!

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.860
Please stop it!

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:19.620
What happened between you and that
yellow, round, fluffy-smelling Gray-tan?

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:21.870
That's because...

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:23.620
That's because?

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:28.130
...you don't own a cellphone, Le Chien?

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.630
I-I see. A cellphone...

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:37.380
If I have a cellphone,
I'll be able to call Gray-tan.

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.970
I'm gonna go sign up
for a cellphone right now!

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.100
No, no, no.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:45.100
The cellphone shop is already closed
for the day. Let's go!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.100
Gray-tan... G-G-G-Gray-tan... Gray-tan!

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:47.980
Gray-tan!

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:53.030
Big Sister, I feel like I ended up
in an outrageous place.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:58.860
So, can you find the scent?

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:02.370
Yeah. Gray-tan's scent is really wonderful!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.620
It's so soft and fluffy!

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.420
There, there, Svin.

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:17.630
Sir told you to stay away from Gray
as much as possible, didn't he?

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:21.010
I-I'm sorry, Ms. Gray.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:22.810
O-Oh no.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:27.730
It's Sir's scent!

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:40.870
Sir!

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.080
Lord El-Melloi II's Case Files
｛Rail Zeppelin｝ Grace note

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:51.460
It has the power to become gigantic
by eating electricity.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.290
I attempted a cancellation, but...

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:59.590
If it's purely a comparison of power,
I'm no match against it.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:01.590
Where is this thing now?

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.300
I did drive it back.

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:05.470
I'd like to say it was a draw,

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.230
but I probably only deterred it for now.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:10.770
That thing...

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:12.900
Flat...

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:15.940
Take the mana balance...

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:18.240
and rever...

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:20.700
Sir!

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.990
It's all right. He just passed out.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.120
Then, I guess
we're taking over from here.

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:25.870
Right.

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:28.410
In that case, Le Chien,
take Sir to the hospital.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.790
Why do I get that job?

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.670
And don't call me "Le Chien"!

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:35.250
If we're dealing with an astral body,
we'll need Gray's powers here.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:36.670
Besides,

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:40.510
didn't Sir tell you
not to be too close to Gray?

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.350
All right.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.600
But make sure to not put
one scratch on Ms. Gray.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.230
At any cost.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.520
Leave it to me!

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:06.990
- Um...
- What's wrong?

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:10.500
Does Svin dislike me?

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.120
He's always glaring at me,

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:17.250
and he breathes so hard
when he looks at me.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:19.670
He doesn't seem to stay calm
around me, either.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:24.840
I don't think Le Chien dislikes you, Gray.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.220
Is that so?

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:30.220
Well, he's not good
at his sense of distance with others.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.640
Though, you're done for
if I'm the one saying this!

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:35.350
For me,

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:40.070
whether it was home or the Clock Tower,
nobody ever took me seriously.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:44.150
Sir and my classmates
were the only ones who called me a fool

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.660
and treated me like a decent human.

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:51.620
Treated like a human...

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:53.790
And it's not just me.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.460
Le Chien and everyone else...

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:01.510
Without Sir, I'm sure
we would've all just been deviates.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:06.300
Yes. Sir does always
watch out for all of us.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:11.890
So well, Le Chien is like that,
and I'm like this!

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:13.770
That's something
you just have to give in.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.850
Wait, am I saying something good here?

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:21.980
Well, let's hurry up and defeat
this monster and go back to see Sir.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:23.690
Yes! Let's go!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.120
Svin...

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:39.000
Sir, please don't talk. I'll call
for the doctor right away.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:42.050
Before a doctor, hand me the phone.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.380
There's a place I need to contact.

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:51.260
This is...

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:54.640
The rodent control guy
Sir was talking about.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:59.940
It's a fresh skeleton!
Only the flesh were bitten off!

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.230
There's another one over there.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:05.360
Looks like feeding grounds.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:09.820
It's here.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:11.410
I found it.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:17.210
- Here goes! Just like what we planned!
- Okay!

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.000
It fell for it!

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:33.010
Now!

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:35.180
<i>First stage restraint rescinded!</i>

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:49.240
This is...

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:52.160
Just like what Sir said.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:55.240
A bounded field is up from the underground
Magical Energy and this thing.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:59.000
So, if we take that flow
and let it run wild, then reverse it...

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.000
Then, farther down from here...

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.550
Yep. We should find the monster's lair.

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:08.760
Let's go!

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:14.850
This is a Mage's workshop, isn't it?

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:17.520
That bunny came from here

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:20.270
to bring the food it pilfered
back to its owner.

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:21.770
Food...

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:24.860
I don't really get it,
but I don't think it's anything good.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:27.360
Those are some words.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:30.400
How dare you trouble me?

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:32.490
Hey there! Sorry for the disturbance!

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:35.080
We knocked, but you didn't hear it, huh?

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:39.580
You barge into
Gueldoa Davenant's Workshop,

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:42.960
and you call that "knocking"?

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:46.050
Who are you nobodies?

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:49.840
Yep! We're here
from Lord El-Melloi II's class!

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:52.090
We're Flat Escardos and Gray!

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:54.550
Lord El-Melloi II?

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:58.140
That so-called upstart
from Modern Magecraft Theories?

00:15:58.140 --> 00:15:59.810
Don't be so rude to him!

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.350
Rude?

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:04.060
Sir is not just some upstart!

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:08.610
He's the best upstart in the Clock Tower
who rose to Lord in his own lifetime!

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:16.240
So, the apprentice of that upstart is here
to destroy a product of my workshop.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:19.450
That's because that monster
is taking innocent people!

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:20.910
Innocent?

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:28.380
Tens of thousands of ordinary lives
are simply fuel for me to reach the Root!

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:32.760
You have infiltrated my workshop
because of such a petty affair?

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:37.050
Human lives are more important than Earth!

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.600
Besides, human lives aren't all too effici—

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:41.640
My objective is not to kill!

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:44.940
I'm saying it's merely
a part of the process!

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:51.530
This time, you don't have
the assistance of your mentor, rookies.

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:54.990
I shall tear out your limbs
and rip out your organs,

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:58.450
then expose the sins of your mentor!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.700
Modern Magecraft is nothing more
than the technique of a thief!

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:04.290
This doesn't look good.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:08.000
I'll put up a flashy show,
so you flee in the meanwhile, Gray!

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:08.840
Huh? But...

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:12.130
I always wanted to say
something like that!

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:13.510
No need for that.

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:20.850
O-Ouch.

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:24.560
Can't you handle things
a bit gentler, Svin?

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:26.560
I'm sorry.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.570
Your orders were to go at full speed.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.230
Well, yeah.

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:33.570
You must be...

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.820
Lord El-Melloi II.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:39.830
So, you're Sir Gueldoa Davenant.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.200
Indeed.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:44.160
Are you here to apologize
for mismanagement of your apprentices?

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.330
You must be joking.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:49.170
I am here to denounce your crimes...

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.710
and to rescue my apprentices over there.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.510
"Crimes," you say?

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:57.720
Your Magecraft utilizes
lightning and a furry creature.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:01.310
In other words, it falls
under the realm of Jupiter.

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:03.310
How do you know that?

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.230
You took a Phantasmal
with elements of Jupiter,

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:09.310
in other words, a rabbit monster,
to collect lightning,

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:12.570
and then converted that
into the power of Thunder God Zeus.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:16.320
This altar is a Code for you
to seize control over others!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:17.910
Damn you!

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.280
I've heard one of the authorities
in Zoology was assassinated,

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.910
and the battle for his position
has intensified.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:26.540
Is what you seek distinction
using Zeus's powers?

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.080
How do you know so much?

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:32.380
I see! You must be using
your apprentices to steal my research!

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:33.670
Who sent you here?

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:38.130
Hardly. Any incompetent fool
would understand with one look here.

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:40.640
Even a talentless substitute Lord.

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:43.100
And this is the electricity
consumption for this district.

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:45.680
It's clearly high.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.980
Enough to run a small factory.

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:52.310
Oh, I see! It's the food
for this electric bunny!

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:53.730
Exactly.

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:56.240
And this is a newspaper article

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:58.990
about the serial murders happening around here.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.530
"The case of the missing people on Druid Street!

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:03.410
Is it a modern day Jack the Ripper?"

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.910
So, what of that, you say?

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:09.920
It may have been possible in the 20th century,
but we live in an information society.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:12.880
If you piece all the information together,

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:16.170
you can immediately tell
there is something here.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:19.380
I will take the liberty
of restraining you, Sir Gueldoa.

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:22.140
You trampled upon
the biggest taboo of Clock Tower.

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.260
Concealment of the Mystics!

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.640
With just this much?

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:29.440
With just this much!

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:32.650
There is no way the Mystics
will come out into the open!

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:34.650
I suggest you refrain from doing that!

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:38.280
I've already indicted you
with the Policies Department,

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:40.360
and Zoology has accepted it!

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:45.910
Everyone at Zoology was highly pleased
that you'll be losing your position.

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:48.370
I...

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.830
My Magecraft!

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:54.420
My grand Code!

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:58.340
All of this would be trivial
a hundred years ago!

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:04.350
A hundred years ago, you would've
simply been an ordinary Mage.

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:07.180
This is what modern times entail.

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:13.480
We at Norwich exist to bring harmony
between Magecraft and modern times.

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:27.990
We've been spared.

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:31.580
Half of all that was a bluff.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:35.420
Honestly, if Sir Gueldoa
had resorted to brute force,

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:37.630
I wouldn't have been able
to do anything.

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:39.170
Was that the case?

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:42.300
I thought you had some sort of plan.

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:47.100
A cowardly thief sneaks away
in the night.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:51.560
If you stride away, bursting with song,
then you are a conquering king.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:54.140
I've never seen that movie.

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:57.400
Those are the words spoken
by some fool in the past.

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:03.650
At times, acting dignified brings better results
than what you're actually possible...

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:05.160
of...

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.070
Sir!

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:10.080
But I've had enough.

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:13.330
Things like this just are not...

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:14.830
my style.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:17.500
Sir,

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:21.010
thank you for all the hard work tonight.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:27.050
EPISODE 3: Thunder and the Underground Labyrinth

00:22:57.980 --> 00:22:59.900
Please feel free to eat away!

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:02.270
Sir, you are the savior of this shop.

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:06.150
I didn't know college professors
captured rats, as well.

00:23:06.530 --> 00:23:08.360
Well, that's how it goes.

00:23:10.450 --> 00:23:13.200
This is tasty! Now, I'll be able
to concentrate on my paper!

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:16.910
Elder Brother, you really have a simple brain.

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:17.620
Shut up!

00:23:17.910 --> 00:23:21.960
You came all the way here
during lunchtime! What do you want?

00:23:22.330 --> 00:23:27.260
I came all the way here to inform you
of what I had Luvia investigate.

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:29.180
It's sad news, though.

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:31.890
The Holy Grail War, was it?

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:36.220
Apparently, two positions for Association
participants have now closed.
